{%- comment -%}
  Carbon speed fixes (owner 2026-10-20) — rendered in <head> right after
  carbon-shield. CSS only.

  Hidden loading spinners: the theme hides its loading overlays with
  opacity:0 (product cards, the Add to Cart button, …) but leaves them
  displayed, so every spinner ran its two infinite animations (rotate +
  stroke-dashoffset — which the GPU cannot take over) forever: 48 at once on a
  collection page, plus the Add to Cart button on every product page.
  Measured on a throttled phone: the CPU was busy ~100% of the time a shopper
  just looked at a collection; with this, ~28%. A spinner still spins while its
  form / button / card is actually loading (.loading or [loading=true]).
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .product-card .product-card-quickview:not(.loading) .loading-overlay { visibility: hidden; }
  .loading-overlay:not(.loading .loading-overlay, [loading="true"] .loading-overlay) .spinner,
  .loading-overlay:not(.loading .loading-overlay, [loading="true"] .loading-overlay) .spinner-path { animation: none; }
</style>
